# FUSE third-party pin: AMD FidelityFX SDK, FSR1 (EASU + RCAS) and CAS subset. Vendored verbatim, no local edits.
# Only the files listed below are vendored: the portable core headers (ffx_core*.h, ffx_common_types.h),
# the FSR1 and CAS GPU headers, the two host headers that declare the effect versions (kept for the pin;
# FUSE does not compile the FidelityFX host runtime), and the Vulkan GLSL pass entry points.
# FUSE uses them two ways: the CPU single-source ports in
# Source/FUSE/Renderer/include/fuse/renderer/upscale/{fsr1,cas}_kernel.hpp transcribe the float32 paths, and the
# fuse_upscale_gpu_reference gate compiles shaders/vk/**.glsl with glslangValidator and runs them on
# Lavapipe to check the ports numerically.
# Checked by `fuse_lint vendored-pins` (ctest: fuse_lint_vendored_pins_fidelityfx).
# To update: re-fetch every file below from the new SDK tag (same paths under sdk/ and the repo root
# LICENSE.txt), then update version, tag, commit, header_version and every sha256 together. sha256 is
# over the file with CRLF normalized to LF.
